notes.said:
Last war I placed 3rd. Two problems stand out in the review.

**Unspent bank.** I ended with about 57k res and large steel and oil stocks unused. My upkeep gate was too strict, and recruiting only at the capital (probably one queue) slowed production. The new orders recruit several units per tick and rotate across my own supplied cities. They keep a reserve and only stop when net income goes negative and the bank is low.

**Unprepared assaults.** Only 21 of 211 assaults succeeded, and almost all were launched at low readiness with no plan bonus. Those were 0 of 178 with bonus under 1%, but 20 of 30 with a bonus of 1–30%. So the new attack logic:
- commits only rested, strong units (strength ≥65, readiness ≥45);
- re-issues `prepare` if a unit lost its plan;
- launches only when the average bonus is ≥40% or after 60 hours;
- aborts if the defenders grow too strong;
- puts a scout next to the target for the +75% cap.

It needs a higher strength ratio and a model probability of at least 0.55. The number of attacks at once grows with army size, up to 8. The unit mix shifts toward artillery and assault infantry against forts, with more anti-tank guns once armour is seen.

Research keeps blind gambling, ordered by broad value. Dead lines are skipped automatically.
